# HEM-7155T (EBK identity): first-time pairing. Omron registers user 2 on this two-user model; OpenPressure
# programs the shared key and reads both banks on the same connection.
# Omron selects HEM-7155T-EBK from the advertised IDs (category 0x0000, model 0x0264);
# OpenPressure maps the Device Information model HEM-7155T-EBK to its HEM-7155T two-bank map.
name hem-7155t/pair
flow pair
register user=2
advertise name=BLEsmart_000002640011223344 services=ecbe3980-c9a2-11e1-b1bd-0002a5d5c51b
# Synthetic Device Information; Omron reads the revisions and the System ID during connection setup.
dis model=HEM-7155T-EBK firmware=0001 software=0001 systemid=0011223344556677
time 2026-01-02T03:04:05 zone=UTC
key 05050505050505050505050505050505

alias unlock b305b680-aee7-11e1-a730-0002a5d5c51b
alias tx db5b55e0-aee7-11e1-965e-0002a5d5c51b,e0b8a060-aee7-11e1-92f4-0002a5d5c51b,0ae12b00-aee8-11e1-a192-0002a5d5c51b,10e1ba60-aee8-11e1-89e5-0002a5d5c51b
alias rx 49123040-aee8-11e1-a74d-0002a5d5c51b,4d0bf320-aee8-11e1-a0d9-0002a5d5c51b,5128ce60-aee8-11e1-b84b-0002a5d5c51b,560f1420-aee8-11e1-8184-0002a5d5c51b
alias clock 00002a2b-0000-1000-8000-00805f9b34fb

# One synthetic record per user, each with sequence number 1 at offset 10 and Omron's record checksum at
# offset 14 (8-bit sum of bytes 0-13; OpenPressure ignores it):
# user 1: 130/78 mmHg, pulse 67, 2025-07-09 06:14:38; user 2: 120/80 mmHg, pulse 70, 2025-08-01 07:30:00.
memory fill=ff
memory 0x98 694e4319261da603 0000 0100 00000000
memory 0x458 5f504619 27208007 0000 0100 0000 dd00
# Index block (index_setting_read_address=10): per user next write position 1 and one unsent record,
# sequence numbers 1 (user 1 at offset 8, user 2 at offset 12), little-endian words.
memory 0x10 0100 0100 0100 0100 01000000 01000000

# Enter key mode, program the key.
write unlock 02 00000000000000000000000000000000
notify unlock 8200
write unlock 00 05050505050505050505050505050505
notify unlock 8000
# OpenPressure follows the pinned omblepy order and unlocks with the new key.
[ours-only: Omron does not follow registration with 01 (docs/protocol.md, observed in the sandbox)] write unlock 01 05050505050505050505050505050505
[ours-only: acknowledgment for the unlock above] notify unlock 8100

write tx 08 00 00 00 00 10 00 18
notify rx 18 80 00 00 00 10 00 01 02 03 04 05 06 07 08 09 0a 0b 0c 0d 0e 0f 00 88

[omron-only: Omron reads the index block (index_setting_read_address) before records] reads 0x10 44 chunk=44
[omron-only: Omron reads setting-info block 3 (index_setting_info_read_address 0x20 + 28)] reads 0x3c 16 chunk=16

[ours-only: OpenPressure imports history during Pair; Omron pairing returns no historical readings (hem-7156t/pair)] reads 0x98 960 chunk=16
[ours-only: OpenPressure imports history during Pair; Omron pairing returns no historical readings (hem-7156t/pair)] reads 0x458 960 chunk=16

[ours-only: OpenPressure clock sync via Current Time; Omron writes setting block 3 instead (docs/omron-sandbox.md)] write clock ea 07 01 02 03 04 05 05 00 01

# Omron's post-pairing settings write for user 2 belongs here (see the exploration transcript).

write tx 08 0f 00 00 00 00 00 07
notify rx 08 8f 00 00 00 00 00 87

[ours-only: OpenPressure imports history during Pair; Omron pairing returns no historical readings] expect reading user=1 sys=130 dia=78 pulse=67 time=2025-07-09T06:14:38
[ours-only: OpenPressure imports history during Pair; Omron pairing returns no historical readings] expect reading user=2 sys=120 dia=80 pulse=70 time=2025-08-01T07:30:00
